    <text>
        <body>
            <div>
                <head>Translated parts</head>
                <p xml:id="T48n2016-start">
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a03.s1" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:02:21.477+09:00">Preface to the Zōng Jiàn Lù</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a05.s1" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:02:21.477+09:00">Written by Yáng Jié, Zuo Cháoqǐng Láng, Shàngshū Lǐbù Yuánwàiláng, Hùjūn</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s1" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:02:21.477+09:00">The true words of all Buddhas</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s2" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:02:21.477+09:00">take the mind as their principle.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s3" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:02:21.477+09:00">Sentient beings believe in the Way</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s4" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:02:21.477+09:00">and take this principle as their mirror.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s5" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:02:21.477+09:00">The realm of sentient beings is the realm of all Buddhas.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s6" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:02:21.477+09:00">Because of delusion, they become sentient beings.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s7" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:02:21.477+09:00">The mind of all Buddhas is the mind of sentient beings.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s8" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:02:21.477+09:00">Because of enlightenment, they become Buddhas.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s9" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:02:21.477+09:00">The mind is like a bright mirror.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s10" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:02:21.477+09:00">All phenomena are clearly reflected.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s11" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:03:32.635+09:00">The Buddha and sentient beings</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s12" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:03:32.635+09:00">are like reflections.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s13" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:03:32.635+09:00">Nirvāṇa and Saṃsāra</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s14" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:03:32.635+09:00">are both merely forceful names.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s15" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:03:32.635+09:00">The essence of the mirror is still and constantly illuminates;</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s16" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:03:32.635+09:00">the light of the mirror illuminates and is constantly still.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s17" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:03:32.635+09:00">Mind, Buddha, sentient beings,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s18" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:03:32.635+09:00">these three are without difference.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s19" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:03:32.635+09:00">In the early years of the kingdom, Chan Master Zhìjué Shòu of Yǒngmíng Monastery in Wúyuè</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s20" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:03:32.635+09:00">realized the highest vehicle,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s21" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:03:32.635+09:00">understood the ultimate meaning,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s22" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:03:32.635+09:00">thoroughly investigated the teachings,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s23" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:03:32.635+09:00">deeply penetrated the Chan sect,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s24" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:03:32.635+09:00">received and upheld the Vinaya,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s25" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:03:32.635+09:00">and extensively performed deeds of benefit.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s26" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:03:32.635+09:00">Because he read in the *Laṅkāvatāra Sūtra* that</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s27" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:03:32.635+09:00">“The Buddha's words take mind as their foundation,”</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s28" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:03:32.635+09:00">he then composed the *Zōngjiàn Lù* (Record of the Source Mirror).</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s29" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:03:32.635+09:00">He raised doubt amidst certainty,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s30" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:03:32.635+09:00">posed questions where there were no questions,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s31" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:03:32.635+09:00">became a friend to those who did not ask,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s32" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:03:32.635+09:00">and was a true great guide.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s33" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:03:32.635+09:00">He cast the treasures of the dragon palace</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s34" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:03:32.635+09:00">and equally bestowed them upon all beings.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s35" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:03:32.635+09:00">He penetrated the barrier of the ancestral school</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s36" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:03:32.635+09:00">and universally welcomed all who came.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s37" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:03:32.635+09:00">When they raised their eyes to look,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s38" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:03:32.635+09:00">all their desires were fulfilled;</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s39" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:04:37.419+09:00">Readily picked up.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s40" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:04:37.419+09:00">All illnesses are healed.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s41" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:04:37.419+09:00">Sweeping away erroneous views.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s42" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:04:37.419+09:00">Pointing towards the wondrous source.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s43" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:04:37.419+09:00">What is meant by "upholding the one mind as the principle."</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s44" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:04:37.419+09:00">"Illuminating the myriad dharmas as a mirror."</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s45" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:04:37.419+09:00">If one takes the Buddha as a mirror,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s46" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:04:37.419+09:00">then one knows that morality (jiè), concentration (dìng), and wisdom (huì) are the principles of all goodness.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s47" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:04:37.419+09:00">Gods (rén tiān), *śrāvakas* (shēng wén), *pratyekabuddhas* (yuán jué), *bodhisattvas*, and *tathāgatas* (rú lái),</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s48" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:04:37.419+09:00">arise from this.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s49" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:04:37.419+09:00">All good beings cannot but believe and accept it.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s50" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:04:37.419+09:00">If one takes sentient beings as a mirror,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s51" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:04:37.419+09:00">then one knows that greed (tān), anger (chēn), and delusion (chī) are the principles of all evil.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s52" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:04:37.419+09:00">*Asuras* (xiū luó), animals, hells, and hungry ghosts,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s53" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:04:37.419+09:00">arise from this.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s54" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:04:37.419+09:00">All evil beings cannot but fear and dread it.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s55" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:04:37.419+09:00">Although good and evil are different,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s56" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:04:37.419+09:00">their principles are the same.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s57" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:04:37.419+09:00">Reflecting back on one's mind,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s58" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:04:37.419+09:00">one knows that it is spiritually bright, deeply still,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s59" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:04:37.419+09:00">vast, all-encompassing, and permeating,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s60" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:04:37.419+09:00">non-active, non-abiding,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s61" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:04:37.419+09:00">without cultivation, without realization,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s62" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:04:37.419+09:00">without dust to be contaminated by,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s63" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:04:37.419+09:00">without impurity to be polished away,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s64" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:04:37.419+09:00">and is the principle of all dharmas.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s65" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:04:37.419+09:00">Initially, King Zhōngyì (忠懿王) of Wú Yuè (吳越)</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s66" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:04:37.419+09:00">wrote a preface for it.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s67" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:16:36.418+09:00">It was kept secret in the Buddhist canon.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a0701.s68" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:16:36.418+09:00">Until the Zhì Yuán and Yuán Fēng periods (1264-1085).</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a2801.s1" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:16:36.418+09:00">The emperor's younger brother, Wèi Duānxiàn Wáng (魏端獻王).</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a2801.s2" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:16:36.418+09:00">Had it carved on woodblocks and distributed to famous monasteries.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a2801.s3" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:16:36.418+09:00">Scholars from all directions.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a2801.s4" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:16:36.418+09:00">Rarely encountered the original copy.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a2801.s5" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:16:36.418+09:00">In the summer of the sixth year of Yuán Yòu (1091).</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a2801.s6" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:16:36.418+09:00">I traveled to the Fǎ Yún Dàochǎng (法雲道場) in Dōng Dū (東都).</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a2801.s7" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:16:36.418+09:00">And first saw the new Qiántáng (錢唐) edition.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a2801.s8" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:16:36.418+09:00">Which was especially refined and detailed.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a2801.s9" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:16:36.418+09:00">It was Wú (吳) man Xú Sīgōng (徐思恭).</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a2801.s10" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:16:36.418+09:00">Who invited Chan Master Fǎ Yǒng (法涌禪師).</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a2801.s11" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:16:36.418+09:00">Along with the elders Yǒnglè (永樂) and Fǎzhēn (法真).</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a2801.s12" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:16:36.418+09:00">To extensively gather various records.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a2801.s13" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:16:36.418+09:00">Using the scriptures of the Three Vehicles.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a2801.s14" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:16:36.418+09:00">And teachings of sages and worthies.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a2801.s15" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:16:36.418+09:00">To proofread and complete it.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a2801.s16" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:16:36.418+09:00">In order to widely disseminate it.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a2801.s17" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:16:36.418+09:00">Its benefit is very broad.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a2801.s18" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:16:36.418+09:00">Fǎ Yǒng knew that I, Yǔ (予), enjoyed reading this record.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415a2801.s19" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:16:36.418+09:00">Therefore, he requested a preface from me.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b07.s1" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:16:36.418+09:00">Preface to the *Zōngjìng Lù* (宗鏡錄).</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b09.s1" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:16:36.418+09:00">Composed by Tiānxià Dà Yuánshuài (天下大元帥) Wú Yuè Guówáng Chù (吳越國王俶).</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s1" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:16:36.418+09:00">In detail.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s2" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:16:36.418+09:00">The teachings within the realm are three.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s3" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:16:36.418+09:00">To rectify the ruler and ministers.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s4" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:16:36.418+09:00">To cherish fathers and sons.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s5" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:16:36.418+09:00">To enrich human relationships.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s6" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">儒 (Rú).</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s7" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">My teacher.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s8" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">Silent and still.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s9" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">Nothing to be seen or heard.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s10" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">From the subtle and profound.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s11" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">Ascending to emptiness.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s12" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">To rest in riding the wind and controlling the scenery.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s13" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">If a ruler obtains it, then he can build firmly and immovably.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s14" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">If a person obtains it, then he can extend blessings without end.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s15" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">道 (Dào).</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s16" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">The teacher of 儒 (Rú).</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s17" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">The Four Noble Truths and the Twelve Links of Dependent Origination.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s18" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">The Three Clarities and the Eight Deliverances.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s19" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">Constantly practicing and never forgetting.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s20" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">Daily cultivating to attain.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s21" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">Once ascending to the stage of fruition.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s22" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">Forever reaching the true and constant.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s23" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">It is the origin of Buddhism and 道 (Dào).</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s24" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">These three teachings only.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s25" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">Are all cultivated from the mind.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s26" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">*Xīn Jìng Lù* (心鏡錄) ("Record of the Mind Mirror").</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s27" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">Written by Zhìjué Chánshī (智覺禪師).</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s28" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">Altogether one hundred scrolls.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1001.s29" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">Encompassing all subtle words.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1801.s1" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">Spoken by the golden mouth of my Buddha.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1801.s2" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">Filling the sea of scriptures.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1801.s3" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">Indeed, it guides and encourages later learners.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1801.s4" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">The wisdom and eloquence of the teacher.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1801.s5" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">Expounding all dharmas.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1801.s6" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">Clearly understanding the one mind.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1801.s7" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">Meditation as vast as a river.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1801.s8" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">Wisdom filling the skies like clouds.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1801.s9" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">Numbering and counting them.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#T48n2016_CBETA_000-0415b1801.s10" xml:lang="en" resp="#gemini-2.0-flash" modified="2025-06-25T11:18:05.364+09:00">Cannot record them all.</seg>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
</TEI>